    <p class="note">Measured 2026-10-24 on the maintainer's machine with Node.js 24.14.0 against telegram 0.6.2: size of the published dist/index.js at gzip -9, median of 11 cold imports, tests and coverage from the v0.6.2 tag. The replay above was run against the same release on that day.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="binaries" class="sec binaries" aria-labelledby="binaries-title">
    <h2 id="binaries-title">Install the release binary</h2>
    <p class="intro">The default way to run <code>ghostpaw-telegram</code>: one executable per platform with Node.js inside, with the same commands and the same MCP server as the npm package. Each line downloads the latest release, checks it against the release&#39;s SHA256SUMS and puts the binary on the PATH (<code>~/.local/bin</code>; the Windows script adds its folder to the user PATH). The default lines never edit <code>~/.profile</code>: <code>export PATH</code> lasts for the current shell only; the labelled <code>~/.profile</code> line keeps it for new shells. Pin a release with <code>--version &lt;x.y.z&gt;</code>; set <code>GHOSTPAW_NO_MODIFY_PATH=1</code> to keep the Windows script from changing the user PATH.</p>
